# ✔ OPTION B: Browser UI Testing (no coding)

Create file:

```
mcp_project/test_page.html
```

Paste:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>
<h3>MCP Pipeline Tester</h3>
<textarea id="prompt" rows="5" cols="50"></textarea><br><br>
<button onclick="send()">Send</button>
<pre id="out"></pre>

<script>
async function send() {
    const prompt = document.getElementById("prompt").value;
    const res = await fetch("http://localhost:5000/ask_llm", {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        body: JSON.stringify({ prompt })
    });
    document.getElementById("out").textContent =
        JSON.stringify(await res.json(), null, 2);
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Now open `test_page.html` → you get a **tester UI in your browser**.

